the%20dynamic%20in%20earnings%20calls%2C%20the%20number%20of%20mentions%20has%20fallen%20from%20early%20and%20mid-year%20peaks.%20Conversely%2C%20there%20have%20been%20just%20eight%20mentions%20of%20a%20%26quot%3BC%20shape%26quot%3B%20in%20the%20past%20two%20years.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%20data-script%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fdatawrapper.dwcdn.net%2FJ8UmQ%2Fembed.js%5C%22%20data-styles%3D%5C%22default-width%5C%22%20data-embed-type%3D%5C%22custom%5C%22%20data-type%3D%5C%22embed%5C%22%3E%3Cdiv%3E%3Cdiv%20class%3D%5C%22feedlyNoScript%5C%22%3E%3Cimg%20alt%3D%5C%22Line%20chart%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fdatawrapper.dwcdn.net%2FJ8UmQ%2Ffull.png%5C%22%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%3Cp%3EFinally%2C%20the%20K-shape%20still%20shows%20up%20clearly%20in%20consumer%20spending.%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.atlantafed.org%2F-%2Fmedia%2FProject%2FAtlanta%2FFRBA%2FDocuments%2Fresearch%2Fpublication%2Fpolicy-hub%2F2026%2F05%2F18%2F03-k-shaped-economy-or-not-evidence-from-payments-survey.pdf%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3EA%20study%3C%2Fa%3E%20from%20the%20Federal%20Reserve%20Bank%20of%20Atlanta%20found%20that%2C%20from%202021%20through%20its%20most%20recent%20data%20in%202025%2C%20spending%20among%20the%20top%2040%25%20of%20earners%20grew%20the%20fastest%2C%20while%20spending%20among%20the%20lowest%20quintile%20grew%20the%20slowest.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BI%20think%20that%20in%20general%2C%20high%20income%2C%20high%20wealth%20consumers%20are%20doing%20just%20fine%2C%26quot%3B%20Pancotti%20said.%20%26quot%3BThey%20have%20no%20issue%20buying%20first-class%20airfares%20even%20when%20they%20have%20doubled%20over%20the%20past%20few%20months.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EInstead%2C%20the%20dynamic%20that's%20been%20shaping%20up%20is%20more%20akin%20to%20a%20K%20with%20slightly%20softer%20prongs%3A%20The%20trajectory%20for%20high%20earners%20hasn't%20changed%2C%20and%20the%20lowest%20earners%20are%20seeing%20slightly%20more%20stability.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EUltimately%2C%20trying%20to%20describe%20the%20economy%20with%20a%20letter%20shape%20might%20just%20be%20alphabet%20soup.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BI%20don't%20think%20we're%20in%20a%20K-shaped%20economy%20when%20it%20comes%20to%20the%20consumer%2C%26quot%3B%20said%20Ernie%20Tedeschi%2C%20the%20chief%20economist%20at%20Stripe.%20%26quot%3BBy%20definition%2C%20the%20rich%20always%20have%20more%20money.%20They're%20driving%20some%20amount%20of%20consumer%20spending%20growth%2C%20and%20it%20just%20doesn't%20look%20like%20the%20story%20in%202024%20or%202025%20or%202026%20is%20meaningfully%20different%20from%20any%20other%20solid%20economy%20with%20a%20roughly%204%25%20unemployment%20rate.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fis-economy-still-k-shaped-latest-data-tells-mixed-story-2026-8%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1785953792000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7377fdf9ea6266446ef11d%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fis-economy-still-k-shaped-latest-data-tells-mixed-story-2026-8%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22From%20a%20%26quot%3BK%26quot%3B%20to%20a%20%26quot%3BC%2C%26quot%3B%20policymakers%20and%20economists%20keep%20trying%20to%20define%20the%20economy's%20shape.%20It's%20leading%20to%20alphabet%20soup.%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22jkaplan%40businessinsider.com%20(Juliana%20Kaplan)%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A9%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22ampUrl%22%3A%22%22%7D%2C%7B%22title%22%3A%22Bank%20of%20America%20spends%20more%20than%20%24250%20million%20on%20GLP-1s%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%224000%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Brian%20Moynihan%20sits%20in%20a%20television%20studio%20wearing%20a%20dark%20suit%20and%20purple%20tie.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7379b5f9ea6266446ef12e%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%222666%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EBrian%20Moynihan%20said%20Bank%20of%20America%20spends%20more%20than%20%24250%2C000%20on%20GLP-1s.%3Cp%3EBloomberg%2FGetty%20Images%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3EBank%20of%20America%20spends%20more%20than%20%24250%20million%20on%20GLP-1s%20for%20its%20employees.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3ECEO%20Brian%20Moynihan%20said%20it's%20part%20of%20a%20long-term%20investment%20in%20employee%20health.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EGLP-1s%20are%20not%20only%20transforming%20corporate%20healthcare%20budgets%2C%20but%20also%20introducing%20HR%20nightmares.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fglp-1-boom-winners-beyond-pharma-fashion-plastic-surgery-gyms-2026-4%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EWeight-loss%20drugs%3C%2Fa%3E%20are%20costing%20Bank%20of%20America%20more%20than%20a%20quarter%20of%20a%20million%20dollars%20a%20year.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ECEO%20Brian%20Moynihan%20said%20that%20the%20more%20than%20%24250%20million%20is%20a%20worthwhile%20investment%20in%20benefits%20for%20his%20more%20than%20210%2C000%20employees.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BWe%20see%20a%20great%20impact%20on%20employees%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20told%20CNBC%20on%20Wednesday%20at%20the%20Aspen%20Economic%20Strategy%20Group%20annual%20meeting%2C%20noting%20that%20the%20bank%20has%20other%20health%20initiatives.%20The%20firm's%20annual%20healthcare%20budget%20is%20around%20%242%20billion.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAs%20Moynihan%20sees%20it%2C%20the%20payoff%20is%20in%20short-%20and%20long-term%20health%20benefits%2C%20like%20a%20reduced%20risk%20of%20heart%20disease.%20He%20said%20that%20though%20some%20people%20might%20leave%20Bank%20of%20America%20before%20benefiting%20from%20the%20medication%2C%20%26quot%3Bit's%20still%20the%20right%20thing%20to%20do.%26quot%3B%20The%20firm%2C%20he%20added%2C%20is%20working%20to%20get%20the%20drugs%20as%20cheaply%20as%20possible%2C%20especially%20now%20that%20the%20medication%20is%20available%20as%20pills.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ENot%20all%20employers%20have%20adopted%20the%20same%20strategy.%20Only%2036%25%20of%20companies%20cover%20GLP-1%20costs%20for%20diabetes%20and%20weight%20loss%2C%20according%20to%20a%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ifebp.org%2Fdetail-pages%2Fresource%2Fsurvey%2Fglp-1-drugs--2026-pulse-survey-us%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%202026%20survey%20%3C%2Fa%3Efrom%20the%20International%20Foundation%20of%20Employee%20Benefit%20Plans.%20Some%20big%20employers%2C%20including%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ft.com%2Fcontent%2F8f3b462e-a4dd-489d-90d9-0733f1390bec%3Fsyn-25a6b1a6%3D1%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3EPwC%2C%20have%20reportedly%20%3C%2Fa%3Estopped%20covering%20the%20drugs%20for%20weight%20loss.%20%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EYet%20GLP-1s%20are%20transforming%20more%20than%20corporate%20budgets.%20Business%20Insider's%20Juliana%20Kaplan%20recently%20reported%20on%20how%20employers%20are%20grappling%20with%20demand%20for%20GLP-1s%2C%20as%20well%20as%20the%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fozempic-weight-loss-drugs-causing-awkward-work-conversations-hr-nightmares-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EHR%20nightmares%20%3C%2Fa%3Earising%20from%20the%20drug's%20prevalence%20among%20employees.%20Some%20Americans%20who%20rely%20on%20the%20drugs%20have%20struggled%20to%20pay%20after%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Flost-100-pounds-zepbound-insurance-denials-ozempic-cancer-2026-4%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Echanges%20in%20their%20insurance%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20creating%20a%20precarious%20balancing%20act%20between%20financial%20and%20physical%20health.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%3Cem%3EHave%20a%20tip%20or%20a%20story%3F%20Contact%20this%20reporter%20via%20email%20at%20%3C%2Fem%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22mailto%3Aatecotzky%40insider.com%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cem%3E%3Cu%3Eatecotzky%40insider.com%3C%2Fu%3E%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cem%3E%20or%20Signal%20at%20alicetecotzky.05.%20Use%20a%20personal%20email%20ad